{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["And Yitzhak trembled exceedingly — because he found hair on the smooth part of Yaakov's neck." "Who then — it is a locutional refinement, like איזו in the Talmud: אימא לי איזי, אַתְאוֹרֶש in [French] 'tu te maries'." "He too shall be blessed — because he hurried to hunt game and bring it to me, and also he knew that he did everything at Rivkah's counsel, and she was discerning regarding him that he was worthy of the blessings."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "The abbreviation ב\"ל is resolved here as indicating the Old French gloss language; the phrase 'tu te maries' translates the cited Romance form אַתְאוֹרֶש."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:29.020166720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}